      "blind_answer": 4,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "Nucleic acids are polynucleotides: their monomers are nucleotides (base + sugar + phosphate). Nucleosides lack the phosphate."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u19_t00_2",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        2
      ],
      "blind_answer": 2,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "Cellulose is the structural polysaccharide of plant cell walls, so option 2 is correct. The other pairs have their functions swapped: hormones are messengers, nucleic acids carry genetic information, and carbohydrates (not vitamins) are the chief energy source."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u19_t00_3",
      "published": false,
      "reason": "stage1_flags",
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        4
      ],
      "blind_answer": 4,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "Biomolecules are non-living, vitamins are needed in small amounts, and carbohydrates can be structural (e.g. cellulose), so 1-3 are wrong. Proteins are structural and act as enzymes, so option 4 is correct."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u19_t00_4",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        3
      ],
      "blind_answer": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "A is true: cellulose is a structural carbohydrate in plant cell walls. R is false: carbohydrates such as glucose and starch are major energy sources."
    },
